{
  "views": "views.json",
  "notes": [
    "Each case: an element as a tool is served it, and what a reader of views.json answers: the row's id (null: no row, the type draws as today), the one sentence (null when no row or no field holds anything), and the banners at the head in order. A case with an `order` also names the fields drawn, in the order drawn (layouts.document); a reader compares `order` only where a case gives one.",
    "Matching a pair with its mark is the profile's own reader and its own fixture (room.fixture.json, the charter cases); these cases only test which row wins and what a row gives.",
    "cites: every field a row names (sentence, lead, fold, layout.by), quoted from the page that defines the kind at its line; a reader of this file checks each quote at its line, and that each named field is one the row's type has in the standard.",
    "tables: a table that is not views.json, read by the cases that name it and never by any other. `two-rows-one-kind` is at fault on purpose: two rows hold narrative/Message, which a build of the file refuses. It exists only to pin what a page does with such a table: the first row wins, and the page is drawn. `lead-and-fold` is well formed: its one row names `story` in both lead and fold, which no row of views.json does, to pin that such a field is drawn in the lead, once."
  ],
